# {{ project_name }}

Generated with the [Austial](https://github.com/) CLI -- a NestJS-style, production-ready
web framework for Python, built on FastAPI.

## Project structure

```
src/
├── main.py                  # entry point (mirrors Nest's main.ts)
├── app/
│   ├── app_module.py        # root module (mirrors app.module.ts)
│   ├── app_controller.py
│   ├── app_service.py
│   └── modules/             # one folder per feature
│       └── health/          # GET /health, GET /health/protected
├── shared/                  # used by several modules
│   ├── guards/              # api_key_guard.py
│   └── services/ pipes/ interceptors/ filters/ middleware/ decorators/ dto/
└── templates/               # non-Python assets
    └── email/
tests/
├── unit/
└── e2e/
```

Add what the app needs next to these: `src/config/`, `src/database/` (entities, migrations), `src/jobs/`,
`src/events/`. Cross-cutting code goes in `src/shared/`, never in a feature folder another module reaches into.

> Note: Python can't import filenames containing dots the way Node resolves
> `health.controller.ts`, so Austial uses `health_controller.py` /
> `health_service.py` / `health_module.py` instead -- same one-folder-per-feature
> layout as Nest, just underscore-suffixed file names.

## Running it

```bash
uv sync
cp .env.example .env
uv run austial serve          # http://localhost:8000, auto-reload
# or
uv run python -m src.main
```

- `GET /health` -> terminus-style health check
- `GET /health/protected` -> requires `x-api-key: <API_KEY from .env>`
- `GET /docs` -> Swagger UI (free from FastAPI)

## Generating more artifacts

```bash
uv run austial generate module cats
uv run austial generate controller cats
uv run austial generate service cats
uv run austial generate resource cats   # module + CRUD controller + service + dto
uv run austial generate guard roles --shared    # src/shared/guards/roles_guard.py
uv run austial generate service mailer --shared # src/shared/services/mailer_service.py
```

## Tests

```bash
uv run pytest
```

## Linting, type-checking & pre-commit hooks

```bash
uv run ruff check .      # lint
uv run ruff format .     # format
uv run mypy src tests    # type-check

uv run pre-commit install --hook-type pre-commit --hook-type pre-push
uv run pre-commit run --all-files   # run every hook once, on demand
```

Once installed, `git commit` runs formatting/linting/type-checks automatically,
and `git push` also runs the test suite -- mirroring a typical Nest project's
husky + lint-staged setup.
